  "location": "NSF30.29 FAQ1 vs NSF30.28",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: NSF30.29 FAQ1 vs NSF30.28",
      "summary": "The NSFR FAQ on Level 2A covered bonds says a rating 'above AA–' is required, while NSF30.28 and LCR30.43 accept 'at least AA–', so a covered bond rated exactly AA– gets 15% or 85% RSF depending on which is followed.",
      "impact": "Position: Covered bond rated exactly AA–, 100, unencumbered, other Level 2A conditions met Reading a: 'At least AA–' -> Level 2A, 15%, RSF 15 Reading b: 'Above AA–' -> not Level 2A; non-HQLA by maturity (e.g. 85% if >1y), RSF 85 Difference: RSF 70",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
